# expect-error: param 'x' needs the C type it crosses as
# An untyped param is a dyn, which no C integer holds (INVARIANTS.md
# V1). The typer lets any value through one, so passing it as a C int
# would truncate a tagged word, a string's pointer included, into a
# plausible integer (V7). The declaration is refused instead.
extern t_not32 {x} i32
print [t_not32 5]
